fx2lafw: clear the bulk IN halt after a STALL

With stock libusb on Windows a STALL on EP2 IN leaves the WinUSB pipe
halted: every later transfer times out with 0 bytes until the empty-transfer
limit aborts the acquisition. (sigrok's own Windows builds use a patched
libusb that aborts and recovers the pipe.) Clear the halt when a transfer
reports LIBUSB_TRANSFER_STALL, then resubmit as before.

diff --git a/src/hardware/fx2lafw/protocol.c b/src/hardware/fx2lafw/protocol.c
index 8854f5a..5067adb 100644
--- a/src/hardware/fx2lafw/protocol.c
+++ b/src/hardware/fx2lafw/protocol.c
@@ -448,6 +448,17 @@ static void LIBUSB_CALL receive_transfer(struct libusb_transfer *transfer)
 	case LIBUSB_TRANSFER_COMPLETED:
 	case LIBUSB_TRANSFER_TIMED_OUT: /* We may have received some data though. */
 		break;
+	case LIBUSB_TRANSFER_STALL:
+		/*
+		 * The endpoint is halted (device STALL or a bus error the host
+		 * controller reports the same way). Stock libusb on Windows
+		 * leaves the pipe halted, so every later transfer just times
+		 * out. Clear the halt so the resubmitted transfers can run.
+		 */
+		sr_warn("Bulk IN endpoint stalled, clearing halt.");
+		libusb_clear_halt(transfer->dev_handle, transfer->endpoint);
+		packet_has_error = TRUE;
+		break;
 	default:
 		packet_has_error = TRUE;
 		break;
